{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, I\u2019d make empathy just a little stronger than fear.\n\nNot mind-reading or forcing everyone to agree \u2014 just giving people a natural pause before they judge, dismiss, or hurt someone, where they could genuinely feel: *\u201cOh. This is what life looks like from where they\u2019re standing.\u201d*\n\nI think so much would ripple out from that one shift. Arguments would turn into conversations more often. Leaders would have a harder time treating people like numbers. Strangers online would remember there\u2019s a real person on the other side. Even on a small scale \u2014 a parent with a frustrated kid, a tired driver in traffic, two friends in a disagreement \u2014 that one moment of understanding can change everything that happens next.\n\nThe world would still have conflict and hard problems to solve, but we\u2019d be solving them *with* each other instead of against each other. That feels like the change all the other good changes grow from.\n\nWhat would yours be?",
